@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: the two questions the model-bridging retirement left open — Q2 (the local model) and Q4 (the catalog)
' covers: internal/sbx/host_ollama.go
' covers: internal/provider/models.go
' covers: .claude/skills/sync-models/SKILL.md
'
' TRIMMED 2026-10-17 (repo-simplification.puml N10). The retirement is APPLIED
' (2026-09-09). Its durable design — the decision, the answers to Q1/Q3/Q5/Q6,
' what landed, the harness's-own-var rule, the seeds that name no model and
' the guard tests — lives in the current-state diagram
' _spec/internal/entrypoint/model-alias-bridges.puml. The measured surface
' (45 + 17 files), the four jobs a TSV row did and the second-pass audit are in
' git history (this file before 2026-10-17). What stays here has no code yet.
' Source files point at model-alias-bridges.puml, not here.
'
' ── Q2. WHAT BECOMES OF PROVEO_LOCAL_MODEL? — DEFERRED BY THE OPERATOR ─────
' Recorded answer (2026-09-09): "we will revisit for e2e, full local model
' support". Not answered here.
' MEASURED 2026-10-17, the path today:
'   host   sbx.LocalModelEnv(tag) (internal/sbx/host_ollama.go:32-47) writes
'          PROVEO_LOCAL_MODEL, the Ollama base URL in three dialects,
'          ANTHROPIC_MODEL / ANTHROPIC_SMALL_FAST_MODEL — and ARCHITECT_MODEL,
'          EDITOR_MODEL, SMALL_MODEL = ollama/<tag> (:39-40). No entrypoint
'          reads those three (TestNoEntrypointReadsARoleName): INERT, the
'          successor of the deleted egress localModelArgs. The first thing to
'          remove once Q2 is answered.
'   guest  each def entrypoint selects its own model from PROVEO_LOCAL_MODEL:
'          opencode's configure_opencode_local_model writes .model and
'          .agents.title.model; cecli exports CECLI_*_MODEL; hermes wires its
'          endpoint; claudecode reads ANTHROPIC_MODEL; cursor is refused
'          (vendor-pinned, run.acceptsLocalModel).
'   route  the operator's host Ollama: _spec/internal/sbx/host-inference.puml.
' THE QUESTION: is --local-model a permanent carve-out — the one caller that
' still selects a model, per harness — or does local inference move into the
' agent's own saved config like every other model choice?
'
' ── Q4. WHAT HAPPENS TO THE CATALOG AND ITS SKILL? — NEVER ASKED ───────────
' internal/provider/models.go (knownModels, ModelProvider, CheckModel) and
' .claude/skills/sync-models keep a model-id table current. Since 2026-09-09
' nothing RESOLVES an id. MEASURED 2026-10-17, the catalog still has readers:
'   run.assembleEnv → warnUnknownModel → provider.CheckModel
'     (internal/run/run.go:586-591, helpers.go:66-74) warns when a harness's
'     own *_MODEL value is no known id — validation of the operator's env;
'   posture.RolesLine → provider.ModelProvider (posture.go:226).
' The skill's own text ("This catalog has no reader today", SKILL.md:128) is
' therefore stale.
' THE QUESTION, narrowed by that measurement: retire the catalog and the skill,
' or keep them as VALIDATION — and if so, does validation extend from the
' operator's env to a saved config that names a model that no longer exists?
' Open against: _spec/internal/provider/model-catalog.puml and
' _spec/internal/provider/model-resolution.puml.
title PLANNED — after model bridging (APPLIED 2026-09-09): Q2 the local model, Q4 the catalog

component "**applied**\nno model choice by environment\nmodel-alias-bridges.puml" as DONE <<app>>
database "the agent's own saved config\n(durable home)" as SAVED <<db>>
component "sbx.LocalModelEnv\nPROVEO_LOCAL_MODEL + base URLs\n+ three inert role names" as LOCAL <<error>>
component "def entrypoints\neach selects its own local model" as ENTRY <<app>>
component "internal/provider/models.go\n+ .claude/skills/sync-models" as CAT <<error>>
component "warnUnknownModel\nposture.RolesLine" as READERS <<app>>

DONE ARROW_MAIN SAVED : the replacement
LOCAL ARROW_MAIN ENTRY : Q2 — a carve-out today
CAT ARROW_OPTIONAL READERS : Q4 — readers left
DONE ARROW_OPTIONAL CAT : nothing resolves an id

note bottom of LOCAL
  **Q2 — deferred by the operator.** The three
  role names it still writes are inert. Is the
  carve-out permanent, or does local inference
  move into the agent's saved config?
end note

note bottom of CAT
  **Q4 — never asked.** The catalog still warns
  on an unknown own-var id. Retire it, or keep
  it as validation that also covers a saved
  config naming a model that is gone?
end note
@enduml
